/-!
# Actual circle-equivariant normal coordinates around the fixed curve

The two original toric charts admit explicit compatible real-analytic
normal frames. Their product map descends through the unchanged cusp
quotient and gluing maps. A proved compact-zero-section argument gives
a positive uniform injectivity radius. The resulting round normal
domain is genuinely diffeomorphic to an open subset of the original
threefold, with its native smooth atlas and literal circle action.

The zero section is exactly the preexisting fixed-curve parametrization.
This package makes no claim about the global complement or recognition
of the entire threefold as a sphere.
-/
